  "id": "waterworkssettlingbeds",
  "note": "WATERWORKS SETTLING BEDS: the two open beds behind the Coldwater Waterworks (920,901 and\n921,901), where the Basin's silt settles out before the filters.\n\nThe tiles' prose: a long open concrete bed full of still brown water, with a walkway along the wall\nand a sluice at each end. Gulls on the walkway.\n\nSo it is a low concrete tank filling the tile, its walls a little above the ground, with the water\na hand below the coping: a flat brown sheet. A steel walkway runs along the north wall and\na sluice housing stands at each end, a small concrete hut with a wheel on top. No sign: nothing\nhere is a building with a door, and the plant next door carries the name. Both tiles bind this one\nmodel, so the pair reads as one installation.",
